# Architecture

## Landing page — component-first mirror pattern

```
landing-page/
  app/
    (routes)/
      page-name/
        page.tsx          ← thin shell: imports page component, no JSX logic
  components/
    ui/                   ← Shadcn primitives only, never modified directly
    page-name/            ← mirrors app/(routes)/page-name/ exactly
      PageNameHero.tsx
      PageNameFeatures.tsx
    shared/               ← Navbar, Footer, cross-page reusables
  hooks/                  ← custom hooks when logic > ~15 lines
  lib/
    utils.ts              ← cn() and pure helpers
```

Rule: every `app/**/page.tsx` must have a matching folder under `components/`.

## Frontend app — feature-first

```
frontend/
  app/
    (auth)/               ← protected routes
    (public)/             ← public routes
    api/                  ← Next.js route handlers
  components/
    ui/                   ← Shadcn primitives
    features/
      feature-name/       ← co-locate everything for a feature
        components/
        hooks/
        types.ts
    shared/               ← cross-feature: Navbar, Footer, etc.
  lib/
    db/                   ← Drizzle client + schema
    auth/                 ← Clerk helpers
    api/                  ← typed fetch wrappers
  types/                  ← global types
```

## Backend API — Hono, route-first

```
backend/
  src/
    routes/
      v1/
        users.ts          ← all handlers for a resource in one file
        auth.ts
    middleware/
      auth.ts             ← JWT verification
      rateLimit.ts        ← Arcjet
      logger.ts           ← structured logging
    lib/
      db.ts               ← Drizzle client
      schema.ts           ← Drizzle schema (single file or split by domain)
    types/
      api.ts              ← request/response types
    index.ts              ← Hono entry point
  drizzle/
    migrations/
  tests/
```

## Component rules (React)

- Functional components only, no class components
- One component per file, named export preferred
- Props typed with `interface NomProps` (suffix `Props`)
- Use Shadcn primitives before building custom ones
- `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` for class merging — never string concat
- Extract custom hooks to `hooks/` when logic exceeds ~15 lines
- Server Components by default — `"use client"` only for event handlers / browser APIs

```tsx
// ✅
interface HeroProps {
  title: string
  cta: string
}
export function Hero({ title, cta }: HeroProps) { … }

// ❌
export default function ({ title, cta }: { title: string; cta: string }) { … }
```

## API route rules (Hono)

- Validate every input with Zod before processing
- Return typed responses — never `any`
- Auth middleware on all protected routes
- Rate limiting middleware on all public-facing routes

```ts
// ✅
app.post("/users", authMiddleware, async (c) => {
  const body = CreateUserSchema.parse(await c.req.json())
  const user = await db.insert(users).values(body).returning()
  return c.json({ data: user[0] }, 201)
})
```

## CSS / Design tokens

- All colors, spacing, radii → CSS variables in `app/globals.css`
- Never hardcode hex colors or pixel values in components
- Dark mode via `next-themes` + `ThemeProvider`

## TypeScript

- `strict: true` always
- No `any` — use `unknown` + type guard if needed
- Prefer `const` assertions and `satisfies` over type casting
- Named exports everywhere except Next.js page/layout files
